    "title": "pandas.Period.day — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Period.day#\n\n- Period.day#\n- Get day of the month that a Period falls on. The day property provides a simple way to access the day component of a Period object, which represents time spans in various frequencies (e.g., daily, hourly, monthly). If the period’s frequency does not include a day component (e.g., yearly or quarterly periods), the returned day corresponds to the first day of that period. \n  - Returns:\n    - int\n See also \n  - `Period.dayofweek`\n  - Get the day of the week.\n  - `Period.dayofyear`\n  - Get the day of the year.\n Examples >>> p = pd.Period(\"2018-03-11\", freq='h') >>> p.day 11",
    "markdown_length": 614,
